ideal(String) -- make an ideal using classic Macaulay syntax
************************************************************

  * Function: *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)ideal,
  * Usage: 
        ideal s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, in the form: "f1,f2,...,fr"
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,

Description
===========

Creates an ideal using an abbreviated format. Each polynomial has the form
described in *note Classic: Top,.  The polynomials are separated by commas.
Spaces and newline characters are ignored.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[a..d,x_1..x_4];                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal "a+b2-1,(a+b)(c+d),x[1]-x[2]3"            |
|                                                         |
|             2                                    3      |
|o2 = ideal (b  + a - 1, a*c + b*c + a*d + b*d, - x  + x )|
|                                                  2    1 |
|                                                         |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note poly(String): poly_lpString_rp, -- make a polynomial using classic
    Macaulay syntax
  * matrix(String) (missing documentation)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note ideal(String): ideal_lpString_rp, -- make an ideal using classic
    Macaulay syntax
