monomialIdeal(String) -- make a monomial ideal using classic Macaulay syntax
****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note monomialIdeal: (Macaulay2Doc)monomialIdeal,
  * Usage: 
        monomialIdeal s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, in the form: "f1,f2,...,fr"
  * Outputs:
      * a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,

Description
===========

Creates a monomial ideal using an abbreviated format.  Each polynomial has the
form described in *note Classic: Top,.  The polynomials are separated by
commas. Spaces and newline characters are ignored.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..e];                        |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal "abc,bcd,cde11"    |
|                                          |
|                                       11 |
|o2 = monomialIdeal (a*b*c, b*c*d, c*d*e  )|
|                                          |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R                   |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note poly(String): poly_lpString_rp, -- make a polynomial using classic
    Macaulay syntax
  * matrix(String) (missing documentation)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note monomialIdeal(String): monomialIdeal_lpString_rp, -- make a monomial
    ideal using classic Macaulay syntax
